{"name":"Cub","hex":"#6e5c4b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cub","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Cub Scouts.","A player on the team the \"Chicago Cubs\"."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cub"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Cub","blocks":[{"text":"The Cub is an extant 1915 silent film drama produced by William A. Brady and directed by Maurice Tourneur. The film is based on a 1910 Broadway play, The Cub by Thompson Buchanan, also produced by Brady. This marks the only time stage actress Martha Hedman starred in a film. This film has been recently restored and available for viewing and DVD purchase."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cub"},{"title":"Cub (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cub is a 2014 Belgian horror film and the feature film directorial debut of Jonas Govaerts. Funds for Cub were partially raised through an IndieGoGo campaign and the film had its world premiere on 10 September 2014 at the Toronto International Film Festival. Filming took place during 2013 and stars Maurice Luijten as Sam, a young boy who goes on a camping trip with his fellow Cub Scouts, only to fall afoul of a bloodthirsty poacher."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Cub_2014_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cub_(film)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 4","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating_4.jpg","share":0.613125},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 3","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_